wikipedia_extract: Shinshū Maru (神州丸 or 神洲丸) was a ship of the Imperial Japanese Army
  during World War II. She was the world's first landing craft carrier ship to be
  designed as such, and a pioneer of modern-day amphibious assault ships. During some
  of her operations, she was known to have used at least four cover names, R1, GL,
  MT, and Ryūjō Maru.  During her career, she was outfitted with a dummy forefunnel
  in an effort to disguise her as the submarine tender Taigei, which was converted
  to the light carrier Ryūhō.
